WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:07.290
- [Mark] All right, Marla.

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.470
Marla, where'd you grow up,

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:09.303
where ya from?

00:00:09.303 --> 00:00:11.380
- [Marla] I was born and
raised in Dallas, Texas.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.810
- [Mark] And tell me about your childhood.

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:15.340
You had both your parents growing up?

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:16.710
- Yeah I had great childhood.

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:19.210
I was raised on a thoroughbred ranch

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:21.030
and I had no brothers and sisters,

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:23.094
so I had a really great childhood.

00:00:23.094 --> 00:00:25.240
- [Mark] Wow, that sounds nice.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:27.620
What age were you when
you finally left home?

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:30.870
- I was 18, two weeks
after my 18th birthday.

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:33.140
My best friend and I pretty
much threw some darts

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.179
at a map and decided to come to Hollywood.

00:00:35.179 --> 00:00:38.673
- [Mark] (laughs) And how's that gone?

00:00:38.673 --> 00:00:40.180
- It's gone pretty good.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:42.470
It's been a spree of...

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:44.750
I've traveled across country

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:47.750
and my favorite is Hawaii.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.400
And I didn't get involved with drugs 'til

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.060
I was like in my late 30s,

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:55.130
so I was kinda like a bloomer on that.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:58.280
And I find myself now in Skid Row

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:01.450
strung out on just about everything

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:03.860
and desperate to get into rehab

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:06.763
and it's been quite a
challenge getting in one.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.543
- [Mark] So what drugs
are you using, currently?

00:01:11.544 --> 00:01:16.544
- Fentanyl, heroin, crack
cocaine, weed, and alcohol.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:17.930
- [Mark] So you don't use crystal meth?

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:20.286
- No, I can't stand crystal meth! (laughs)

00:01:20.286 --> 00:01:23.012
- [Mark] (laughs) All right, and do you

00:01:23.012 --> 00:01:24.640
have children of your own?

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:25.870
- Yeah, I have two girls.

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:28.010
I was sober for 12 years in there.

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:33.010
I took a break and got married
and had to two children.

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.370
- [Mark] And there was, so you were using

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:37.710
before that happened,
and then you got clean?

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:38.750
- Right.
- [Mark] How'd you get clean

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:39.957
from some of these drugs?

00:01:39.957 --> 00:01:42.420
- I went to Tarzana Treatment Center

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:43.253
and I stayed clean

00:01:43.253 --> 00:01:45.751
almost 11 years.
(sirens blaring)

00:01:45.751 --> 00:01:47.690
- [Mark] And what got you to relapse?

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:49.250
- I went through a nasty divorce

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:51.913
and just wanted to check out for a while.

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:55.370
I had no idea it was going to

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:57.310
lead me down to Skid Row though.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:00.110
This is pretty traumatic down here.

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:01.400
- [Mark] Yeah, it's pretty horrible.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.630
- Yeah, very horrible down here.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.070
- [Mark] So you're living in a tent?

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:07.868
- Yeah, I live in a tent
on the sidewalk right now

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:10.960
and I've been doing everything
I can to get my housing

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:13.260
but it just goes really slow.

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:16.310
It's really scary down here
for me 'cause I'm by myself

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:19.260
and I'm white, for one, so like they don't

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:20.413
treat me very nice down here.

00:02:20.413 --> 00:02:22.060
They don't treat any while people

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:23.670
very nice down here. (chuckles)

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:25.770
- [Mark] Yeah, you're a minority, for one.

00:02:26.639 --> 00:02:28.350
What are you doing for money now?

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:31.230
- I work on the streets, I prostitute,

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:35.290
and I go in stores and steal things

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:38.920
and bring 'em back and get 50
cents on the dollar for them.

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:44.260
- [Mark] Have you had arrests
for any of this stuff?

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.793
- Yeah, I've gotten
arrested for prostitution.

00:02:50.222 --> 00:02:53.500
Yeah, it's just been one
big nightmare this time.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:55.919
It's not fun like it used to be.

00:02:55.919 --> 00:02:56.939
- [Mark] It was fun at one point?

00:02:56.939 --> 00:02:58.600
- Yeah, at one point it was a lot of fun

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:01.190
to run the streets and run
'em up but it's not anymore.

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:03.083
It's more like survival now.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.410
Yeah, and guys that pick
you up now are pretty crazy.

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:10.223
Some of 'em can be really mean.

00:03:11.069 --> 00:03:15.960
- [Mark] Have you had instances
where they were violent or?

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:17.030
- Oh sure, yeah.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:20.260
I've have 'em pull guns
and knives out on me.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:22.610
Yeah, I've had some pretty
rough things happen.

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:27.410
Yeah, I can't hardly sleep anymore

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.670
'cause I have issues with
sleeping and waking up

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:31.070
and having people in my tent

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:32.620
and doing horrible things to me,

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:35.660
so it's hard for me to sleep now.

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:37.030
- [Mark] Yeah, I've heard that a lot

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:39.540
where women will wake up
with a guy in their tent.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:41.200
- Yeah, a total stranger.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.560
Yeah, it's pretty scary.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:45.133
They do it a lot around here.

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:50.717
- [Mark] How many years
have you been on Skid Row?

00:03:50.717 --> 00:03:53.210
- [Marla] I've been down
here fore six years now.

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:54.043
- [Mark] Six years.

00:03:54.043 --> 00:03:56.130
How do you think that's changed
you, the six years here?

00:03:56.130 --> 00:04:00.150
- [Marla] Oh wow, definitely
made my skin a little tougher

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:01.650
I would have to say and

00:04:03.442 --> 00:04:06.560
just everyday dealing with people is,

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:10.110
everything down here is switched
around, it's so backwards.

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:13.070
When I get on the train
and go to Long Beach

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:15.980
or Hollywood or something, I
have to like reprogram myself

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:19.130
(laughs) 'cause, you know,
the way we live down here

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:21.670
and the way people treat you
and the way you treat people

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:23.960
is totally different down here than,

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:26.544
you know, in the real world.
- Yeah, it's a

00:04:26.544 --> 00:04:27.740
totally different--
- Yeah, everything's pretty

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:29.400
backwards down here.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.100
- [Mark] Do you still have
contact with your kids

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.410
or your family?

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:35.205
- [Marla] My husband, my
ex-husband won't let me

00:04:35.205 --> 00:04:38.620
see or talk to them
while I'm getting loaded,

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:40.770
and my mom is all I have left

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:43.460
and they're all pretty
disappointed with me right now,

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:45.400
so I'm really trying to get into rehab

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.310
'cause I just don't see myself

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:50.143
lasting down here too
much longer, I don't.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:52.650
- [Mark] What do you need in order

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:56.189
to get rehab to work to be clean? I mean--

00:04:56.189 --> 00:04:59.650
- [Marla] Oh, I need some
insurance, some medical insurance,

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:04.350
which I just got, and yeah
like an ID and a social.

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:05.990
Every time I get ID and a social

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:08.620
and stuff my purse gets stolen.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:11.160
It's really rough down here
keeping like credentials

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:13.860
and a cellphone, things
that you really need.

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:15.300
Everyday life that you need,

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:16.580
it's really difficult to keep

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:20.070
a hold of those things down here, yeah.

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:22.450
- [Mark] Everything gets stolen
like almost daily, right?

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:24.820
- Yeah yeah, I've had a hundred phones.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:26.633
I blink and they get stolen.

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:28.930
Yeah, so it's really hard to keep

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:30.730
hold of like family and friends,

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:33.440
keep in touch with them 'cause
I can't keep a cellphone

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:35.663
and yeah, it's just really hard.

00:05:37.614 --> 00:05:38.950
- [Mark] And if you don't do this

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:40.420
the alternative is you end up living

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:42.240
the rest of your life down here?

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:45.450
- Yeah, a lot of my friends
have died down here.

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:48.097
I don't wanna leave in a pine box.

00:05:48.097 --> 00:05:49.550
- [Mark] Doing some of
the drugs you're doing

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:51.350
are pretty dangerous.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:52.633
- Yeah, really dangerous.

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:57.443
You just get to a point where
you don't care sometimes.

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:00.720
And because you're so
isolated from everybody

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:02.645
who cares about you, you start believing

00:06:02.645 --> 00:06:05.370
that nobody cares anymore.

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:07.830
It's just, it's a bunch of
bullshit your head feeds you.

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:09.113
You start to believe it.

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:14.880
- [Mark] And getting clean
from heroin, I've heard--

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:17.620
- It's really hard.
- I've heard it's like,

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:21.820
dying is preferable.
- Yeah, I really wanna do it

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:24.400
but nowadays it rough, you know,

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.063
because of insurance and medical

00:06:26.063 --> 00:06:28.460
and the other type of drugs I'm on

00:06:28.460 --> 00:06:31.110
it's like a really high
risk to get me clean

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:33.260
off of those things without, you know,

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:36.930
me go into seizures or
dying or something so

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:40.330
it's really challenging tryin'
get in to a medical facility

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:43.320
'cause none of them wanna help you

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:44.870
'cause you're such a high risk.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:48.093
- [Mark] All right Marla.

00:06:48.093 --> 00:06:49.195
Well thank you so much for coming in

00:06:49.195 --> 00:06:50.490
and telling me your story and good luck

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:54.194
with getting into rehab and getting clean

00:06:54.194 --> 00:06:55.055
from all this stuff.
- Thank you.

00:06:55.055 --> 00:06:56.233
I'm determined.

00:06:56.233 --> 00:06:58.224
- [Mark] Good for you!

00:06:58.224 --> 00:07:01.641
All right, thank you.
- [Marla] Thank you.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:05.510
I'm so glad you told me to come in,

00:07:05.510 --> 00:07:06.795
asked me if you could come in again.

00:07:06.795 --> 00:07:07.803
This one I'll use.

